{
  "root_node": "model.fct_orders",
  "cause": "code_change",
  "action": "patch",
  "evidence": "The not_null test on fct_orders.region_name failed with 14,625 nulls (total rows 15,000). In fct_orders SQL, region_name is sourced via a left join: `left join {{ ref('dim_customers') }} c on o.order_key = c.customer_key`. This join uses o.order_key instead of o.customer_key, causing only 375 rows to match dim_customers (verified by a join count query) and leaving region_name null for the rest. The upstream tables (raw.orders, staging.stg_orders, dim_customers) have correct row counts and no nulls in region_name, indicating the issue originates in the fct_orders model code. The fix is to patch the join condition to `on o.customer_key = c.customer_key`."
}
